// A section with no time of its own opens at the SCORE meter, not the meter a
// PREVIOUS section changed to mid-way. Section A opens 3/4 (its own pickup) then
// switches to 4/4; section B, stating no time, must reset to the score 4/4 - the
// 3/4 must not leak in. A2 replays A, so its 3/4 pickup returns.
//
// ⚠️ ONE `'` PER SECTION, ON ITS FIRST NOTE. This book's claim is about the METER, and
// its pitches were written by habit: every note carried a `'`, and in relative mode each
// one counts from the NEAREST letter, so the line climbed to octave 12 and nine of its
// notes ran off the top of the MIDI range. Nothing in the suite looked at the pitch of a
// book that never claimed one (2026-08-17).
title "Section meter resets to score"
time 4/4
key c major

part melody { clef treble }

section A { time 3/4 c'4 d e | time 4/4 f4 e d c | d2 e | }
section B { g'4 f e d | c1 | }

form main { A B A "A2" }

score main "meter" { staff melody }
